<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Áed Sláine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 604</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Áed Sláine was a king of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> in Ireland, from whom the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sil-naedo-slaine">Síl nÁedo Sláine</a> descended. Remembered as joint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/high-king-of-ireland">High King of Ireland</a> until his murder in 604, he gave his name to the kindred that established itself in the plain of Brega in the 7th century, ruling the lands around Tara, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knowth">Knowth</a> and Newgrange.</p></div>
